  "title": "The Mug Handle Treaty",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "Two people sharing a tiny table both keep rotating a mug handle into the other’s workspace. They mark a small neutral landing spot between their notebooks, place the mug there after each sip, and discover the table finally has room for a biscuit plate too.",
